# Sennheiser EW-DX Receiver Driver (SSCv2, OpenAPI 1.7)
#
# Controls a Sennheiser Evolution Wireless Digital rack receiver, the EW-DX
# EM 2, EM 2 Dante or EM 4 Dante, over Sennheiser Sound Control Protocol v2
# (SSCv2): a REST API over HTTPS on port 443, JSON bodies, HTTP Basic
# authentication as the fixed user "api" with the third-party password set
# in Sennheiser Control Cockpit. Firmware 4.0 or newer; older firmware speaks
# SSC v1 (JSON over UDP 45), which this driver does not.
#
# Protocol reference (the manufacturer's own):
#   - "EW-DX 3rd-party API", OpenAPI 1.7, the file the Sennheiser 3rd Party
#     API site's Swagger page renders (source_url below). This is the
#     defining document for every path, field, range, enumeration and status
#     code here. Archived in the workspace as
#     driver-roadmap/reference-docs/sennheiser-ewdx-openapi-1.7.yaml.
#   - "Sennheiser 3rd Party API" v6.2 (08/2026): the SSCv2 specification
#     2.3 (subscriptions, dynamic resources, notification syntax) and the
#     product pages. docs.cloud.sennheiser.com/en-us/api-docs/
#
# Not hardware-verified: built from the documents above and checked against
# the simulator below. What the documents leave open is listed in the
# workspace record (driver-roadmap/shipped/sennheiser_ewdx.md).
#
# Push, not polling (SSCv2 spec, "SSCv2 subscriptions"):
#   The receiver streams every change of a subscribed resource as a
#   Server-Sent Event. The stream is a session: GET
#   /api/ssc/state/subscriptions opens it, the reply's Content-Location
#   header (and the "open" event) names the session, and a PUT of a
#   resource-path list to /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{id}/add arms it.
#   The receiver then sends the current value of every listed resource and
#   each later change, from its front panel, Control Cockpit or the API.
#   The push block's session handshake does that here: the register list
#   runs once per (re)open, so a reopen (the device's "close" event, a
#   dropped stream, 300 s of silence) is also a full resync. Polling stays
#   on at 30 s for the device-level resources only, as the liveness
#   baseline; per-channel and transmitter state comes from the session,
#   because a channel's own GET body carries no channel number to route by.
#
#   The subscription is split into one request per resource group so that a
#   list the receiver refuses (a resource its firmware lacks) costs only that
#   group. The per-channel groups follow the roster, and the roster follows
#   the receiver's own product code (2 or 4 channels) read from
#   /api/device/identity before the per-channel groups run, so a two-channel
#   receiver is never asked for channels 3 and 4.
#
#   The transmitter list /api/transmitters is a control resource: one
#   subscription to it covers /api/transmitters/{n}, /battery and /warnings
#   for every linked transmitter, including ones linked later (SSCv2 spec,
#   "Dynamic Resource Subscriptions"). A transmitter that unlinks is
#   reported as null, which reads as tx_linked false.
#
#   The four RF and audio meters per channel are FastResource feeds the spec
#   says to subscribe only while the data is in use: "Report Level Meters"
#   arms them on connect, and the Channel Meters On/Off commands switch them
#   at runtime. They are throttled to two updates a second per channel and
#   relay to the cloud at low priority.
#
# Why YAML:
#   Everything on the wire is JSON over HTTPS with Basic auth, and the push
#   block's session handshake (platform 0.34.0) is the subscription
#   mechanism, so nothing needs code. The TeamConnect Ceiling Medium driver
#   is the same protocol in Python, written before the handshake was
#   declarative.
#
# Channels are child entities (local ids 1..4, wire channelId 0..3). Each
# carries its receiver settings, its RF and audio state, its sync settings
# (what the receiver writes into a transmitter on a sync) and the linked
# transmitter's own state and battery, because a transmitter belongs to
# exactly one channel on this API.
#
# Scope: every resource the EW-DX OpenAPI 1.7 declares except the raw
# address tree (/api/ssc/schema), the open-source licence download, and the
# frequency-bank reads (arrays of kHz values with nowhere to land as flat
# state; the user bank is still writable).

id: sennheiser_ewdx
name: Sennheiser EW-DX Receiver
manufacturer: Sennheiser
category: audio
version: 1.0.0
# The push block's session handshake, its register list and the json
# `contains` mapping all arrived in 0.34.0.
min_platform_version: "0.34.0"
author: OpenAVC
description: >
  Evolution Wireless Digital rack receivers (EW-DX EM 2, EM 2 Dante,
  EM 4 Dante) over SSCv2, the HTTPS REST API with Server-Sent Events.
  Per-channel mute, gain and output level, RF frequency and presets,
  warnings (no link, low signal, RF and AF peak, encryption), the linked
  transmitter's mute, battery and warnings, sync settings, opt-in RF and
  audio meters. Every change streams in as it happens.

source_url: https://docs.cloud.sennheiser.com/en-us/api-docs/api-docs/open-api-ew-dx.html
tags: [sennheiser, ew-dx, evolution-wireless, wireless-microphone, receiver, dante, sscv2]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [sscv2]
ports: [443]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sennheiser
    models:
      - EW-DX EM 2
      - EW-DX EM 2 Dante
      - EW-DX EM 4 Dante
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Built from Sennheiser's SSCv2 specification and the EW-DX OpenAPI 1.7
      schema (firmware 4.0 or newer; earlier firmware speaks SSC v1 and is
      not covered). Not yet run against a receiver. The transmitters (EW-DX
      SK, SK 3-pin, SKM, SKM-S, the TS 3-pin and 5-pin table stands, and
      the EW-D SK, SKP and SKM-S) are reported through the receiver channel
      they are linked to.

help:
  overview: >
    Controls a Sennheiser EW-DX rack receiver and shows what its wireless
    microphones are doing. Each receiver channel reports the linked
    transmitter's battery, RF signal and warnings, so a panel can show a
    rack at a glance and a trigger can alert on a flat battery or a lost
    link. Mute channels, set gain and output level, recall frequency
    presets, and write the sync settings a transmitter picks up when it is
    held to the receiver. Everything the receiver changes, from its front
    panel or Control Cockpit, shows up here as it happens.
  setup: >
    1. Set the receiver up once in Sennheiser Control Cockpit and update it
       to firmware 4.0 or newer (the API arrived with 4.0).
    2. On the receiver's device page in Control Cockpit, enable third-party
       access and set a third-party password.
    3. Enter the receiver's IP address and that password here. The user name
       is always "api". Set "Receiver Channels" to 4 for an EM 4; the
       receiver corrects the count itself once connected.
    4. Turn on "Report Level Meters" only if a panel shows RF or audio
       levels. They are continuous feeds, so they stay off unless needed;
       a macro can also switch them per channel.
  connection: >
    HTTPS on port 443 with the third-party password from Control Cockpit.
    The receiver's own certificate is self-signed, so certificate
    verification is off unless you turn it on. A receiver on firmware
    older than 4.0 has no HTTPS API at all.

discovery:
  # /api/device/identity answers without credentials (its OpenAPI entry
  # declares no security), and only an EW-DX receiver answers with a product
  # code starting EWDX. HTTPS only, self-signed, so the probe is a TLS GET.
  tcp_probe:
    port: 443
    tls: true
    send_ascii: "GET /api/device/identity HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: ewdx\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
    expect_regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"EWDX'
    extract_manufacturer: "Sennheiser"
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '"product"\s*:\s*"(EWDX[A-Z0-9]+)"'
        group: 1
  # Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG (IEEE registry).
  oui:
    - "00:1b:66"
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sennheiser"

transport: http

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 443
  ssl: true
  verify_ssl: false
  auth_type: "basic"
  username: "api"
  password: ""
  timeout: 5.0
  poll_interval: 30
  channel_count: 2
  enable_meters: false

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
    help: "The receiver's IP address, as shown in Control Cockpit."
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 443
    label: HTTPS Port
    advanced: true
    help: "443 on every receiver; change it only behind a port forward."
  password:
    type: string
    secret: true
    required: true
    label: Third-party Password
    help: >
      The third-party password set on the receiver's device page in
      Sennheiser Control Cockpit. The user name is always "api" and needs
      no entry.
  verify_ssl:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Verify TLS Certificate
    advanced: true
    help: >
      Off by default: the receiver ships a self-signed certificate. Turn on
      only if a trusted certificate has been installed on it.
  channel_count:
    type: integer
    default: 2
    min: 2
    max: 4
    label: Receiver Channels
    help: >
      2 for an EM 2, 4 for an EM 4. Only the starting point: once connected
      the receiver reports its own channel count and the roster follows it.
  enable_meters:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Report Level Meters
    help: >
      Streams each channel's RF signal strength, RF quality, diversity and
      audio level. Off by default because it is a continuous feed; a macro
      or panel can also switch it per channel with the Channel Meters
      On/Off commands.

# ── Push: the SSCv2 subscription session ──────────────────────────────
# One stream, named by the receiver; the register list arms it on every
# (re)open. query_identity comes first so the roster is sized from the
# receiver's own product code before the per-channel groups run.
push:
  type: sse
  path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions
  # The receiver documents no keepalive. A reopen after five quiet minutes
  # is a new session the receiver answers with every value, so a silent
  # rack gets a free full resync and a half-open stream is noticed.
  idle_timeout: 300
  session:
    header: Content-Location
    event: open
    key: sessionUUID
    pattern: "([0-9a-fA-F-]{36})$"
    close_event: close
  register:
    - query_identity
    - subscribe_device
    - { command: subscribe_channel, each_child: channel }
    - subscribe_transmitters
    - { command: channel_meters_on, each_child: channel, when: enable_meters }
  unregister: end_subscription

quick_actions: [identify_on]
actions:
  - id: identify_on
    icon: eye
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.identifying", operator: falsy }
  - id: identify_off
    icon: eye-off
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.identifying", operator: truthy }

state_variables:
  # ── Identity ──
  product:
    type: string
    label: Product Code
    help: "The product code the receiver identifies itself by (EWDX2CHS, EWDX2CHDS, EWDX4CHDS)"
  model:
    type: string
    label: Model
  channel_count_reported:
    type: integer
    label: Receiver Channels
    help: "Read from the product code; sizes the channel roster"
  serial:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
  hardware_revision:
    type: string
    label: Hardware Revision
  vendor:
    type: string
    label: Vendor
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "Set in Control Cockpit; read-only on this API"
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
  position:
    type: string
    label: Position

  # ── Device state ──
  device_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["Normal", "Identifying", "FirmwareUpdate", "Busy"]
    label: Device State
    help: "Busy while the receiver starts, applies a long operation or restarts"
    cloud_priority: high
  device_warning_count:
    type: integer
    label: Device Warnings
    help: "How many device-wide warnings the receiver reports"
  identifying:
    type: boolean
    label: Identifying
    help: "The receiver's display is flashing to show which unit this is"
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
  dante_version:
    type: string
    label: Dante Firmware Version
  firmware_update_state:
    type: enum
    values: ["Idle", "Updating"]
    label: Firmware Update
    cloud_priority: high
  firmware_update_progress:
    type: integer
    label: Firmware Update Progress
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  firmware_last_status:
    type: string
    label: Last Firmware Update Result
  ssc_protocol_version:
    type: string
    label: SSC Protocol Version
  ssc_schema_version:
    type: string
    label: API Schema Version

  # ── RF ──
  rf_code:
    type: enum
    values: ["Q1-9", "R1-9", "S1-10", "S2-10", "S4-10", "U1/5", "V3-4", "V5-7", "Y1-3"]
    label: Frequency Range Code
    help: "The country-specific frequency variant of this receiver"
  rf_range_count:
    type: integer
    label: Frequency Ranges
    help: "How many tuning ranges the receiver has; some variants have gaps"
  rf_range_start_khz:
    type: integer
    label: Tuning Range Start
    unit: kHz
  rf_range_end_khz:
    type: integer
    label: Tuning Range End
    unit: kHz
  rf_range_step_khz:
    type: integer
    label: Tuning Step
    unit: kHz
  transmission_mode:
    type: enum
    values: ["Standard", "LinkDensity"]
    label: Transmission Mode
    help: "Link Density mode doubles the channel count in a crowded spectrum"
  preset_spacing_khz:
    type: integer
    label: Preset Spacing
    unit: kHz
  encryption_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: AES-256 Encryption
    cloud_priority: high
  legacy_mode_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: SSC v1 Legacy Mode
    help: "Whether the receiver still answers the unencrypted SSC v1 protocol on UDP 45"

child_entity_types:
  channel:
    label: "Channel"
    label_plural: "Channels"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 4
    instances:
      # The receiver reports its channel count in its product code, so the
      # roster follows the hardware once connected; channel_count is only
      # the offline fallback.
      count_from_state: channel_count_reported
      count_from: channel_count
      label: "Channel {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "mute", "tx_linked", "tx_battery_percent", "no_link", "low_signal"]
    state_variables:
      # ── Receiver channel ──
      name:
        type: string
        label: Channel Name
        help: "Up to eight characters, as shown on the receiver's display"
      mute:
        type: boolean
        label: Mute
        help: "Audio output mute of this receiver channel"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      gain:
        type: integer
        label: Gain
        min: -3
        max: 42
        step: 3
        unit: dB
        control: true
      output_level:
        type: integer
        label: AF Output Level
        min: -24
        max: 18
        step: 6
        unit: dB
        control: true
      mate:
        type: enum
        values: ["TX1", "TX2", "TX3", "TX4"]
        label: Mate Slot
        help: "The transmitter slot this channel is paired with"
      audio_output:
        type: enum
        values: ["Out1", "Out2", "Out3", "Out4"]
        label: Audio Output
        help: "The receiver output this channel feeds"
      identifying:
        type: boolean
        label: Identifying
        help: "The channel's display is flashing to show which channel this is"

      # ── Warnings ──
      aes256_error:
        type: boolean
        label: "AES-256 Error"
        help: "The receiver and transmitter disagree on encryption, so no audio passes"
        cloud_priority: high
      low_signal:
        type: boolean
        label: "Low RF Signal"
        help: "The transmitter's signal is weak"
        cloud_priority: high
      no_link:
        type: boolean
        label: "No Link"
        help: "No transmitter is linked to this channel"
        cloud_priority: high
      rf_peak:
        type: boolean
        label: "RF Peak"
        help: "The RF input is overloaded"
        cloud_priority: high
      af_peak:
        type: boolean
        label: "AF Peak"
        help: "The audio level is clipping"
        cloud_priority: high

      # ── RF ──
      frequency_khz:
        type: integer
        label: Frequency
        unit: kHz
        control: true
      preset_type:
        type: enum
        values: ["Factory", "User", "None"]
        label: Active Preset Type
        help: "None when the frequency was set directly rather than from a preset"
      preset_bank:
        type: integer
        label: Active Preset Bank
      preset_channel:
        type: integer
        label: Active Preset Channel

      # ── Meters (opt-in feed) ──
      rssi_dbm:
        type: number
        label: RF Signal Strength
        min: -107
        max: 0
        unit: dBm
        cloud_priority: low
      rsqi_percent:
        type: number
        label: RF Signal Quality
        min: 0
        max: 100
        unit: "%"
        cloud_priority: low
      diversity:
        type: integer
        label: Diversity Indicator
        min: 0
        max: 2
        help: "Which antenna path the receiver is using"
        cloud_priority: low
      level_dbfs:
        type: number
        label: Audio Level
        min: -138.5
        max: 0
        unit: dBFS
        cloud_priority: low

      # ── Sync settings: what the receiver writes into a transmitter on a sync ──
      sync_mute_config:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "RfMute", "AfMute"]
        label: Sync Mute Mode
        help: "What a handheld or bodypack's mute switch does after a sync"
      sync_cable_emulation:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "Type1", "Type2", "Type3"]
        label: Sync Cable Emulation
      sync_lowcut:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "30Hz", "60Hz", "80Hz", "100Hz", "120Hz"]
        label: Sync Low Cut
      sync_lock:
        type: boolean
        label: Sync Lock
        help: "Lock the transmitter's controls after a sync"
      sync_trim:
        type: integer
        label: Sync Trim
        min: -12
        max: 6
        unit: dB
      sync_led:
        type: boolean
        label: Sync LED
      sync_mute_config_ts:
        type: enum
        values: ["AfMute", "Off", "PTT", "PTM"]
        label: Sync Table Stand Mute Mode
        help: "What a table stand's button does after a sync: push to talk or push to mute"
      sync_ignore_mute_config:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Mute Mode"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's mute mode alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_cable_emulation:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Cable Emulation"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's cable emulation alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_lowcut:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Low Cut"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's low cut alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_lock:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Lock"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's lock alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_trim:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Trim"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's trim alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_led:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips LED"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's led alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_name:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Name"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's name alone on a sync"
      sync_ignore_frequency:
        type: boolean
        label: "Sync Skips Frequency"
        help: "Leave the transmitter's frequency alone on a sync"

      # ── Linked transmitter ──
      tx_linked:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter Linked
        help: "A transmitter is linked to this channel and reporting"
        cloud_priority: high
      tx_type:
        type: enum
        values: ["EW_D_SKP", "EW_D_SK", "EW_D_SKM_S", "EW_DX_SK", "EW_DX_SK_3_PIN", "EW_DX_SKM", "EW_DX_SKM_S", "EW_DX_TS_3_PIN", "EW_DX_TS_5_PIN"]
        label: Transmitter Type
      tx_capsule:
        type: enum
        values: ["Unknown", "KK_205", "KK_204", "ME_9002", "ME_9004", "ME_9005", "MME_865", "MD_9235", "MM_435", "MM_445", "MMD_945", "MMD_935", "MMD_845", "MMD_835", "MMD_815_1", "MMK_965", "MMD_42_I", "None"]
        label: Capsule
      tx_name:
        type: string
        label: Transmitter Name
      tx_version:
        type: string
        label: Transmitter Firmware
      tx_mute:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter Mute
        help: "The transmitter's own mute switch"
        cloud_priority: high
      tx_identifying:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter Identifying
      tx_lowcut:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "30Hz", "60Hz", "80Hz", "100Hz", "120Hz"]
        label: Transmitter Low Cut
      tx_trim:
        type: integer
        label: Transmitter Trim
        min: -12
        max: 6
        unit: dB
      tx_cable_emulation:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "Type1", "Type2", "Type3"]
        label: Transmitter Cable Emulation
      tx_led:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter LED
      tx_lock:
        type: boolean
        label: Transmitter Locked
      tx_mute_config:
        type: enum
        values: ["Off", "RfMute", "AfMute"]
        label: Transmitter Mute Mode
      tx_mute_config_table_stand:
        type: enum
        values: ["AfMute", "Off", "PushToTalk", "PushToMute"]
        label: Table Stand Mute Mode
      tx_battery_type:
        type: enum
        values: ["Battery", "PrimaryCell", "NoBattery"]
        label: Battery Type
        help: "A rechargeable pack, primary cells, or none reported"
      tx_battery_minutes:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Runtime
        unit: min
        cloud_priority: high
      tx_battery_percent:
        type: integer
        label: Battery Level
        min: 0
        max: 100
        unit: "%"
        cloud_priority: high
      tx_low_battery:
        type: boolean
        label: "Low Battery"
        help: "The transmitter's battery is nearly flat"
        cloud_priority: high
      tx_af_peak:
        type: boolean
        label: "Transmitter AF Peak"
        help: "The transmitter's audio input is clipping"
        cloud_priority: high

commands:
  # ── Queries (polled; the session covers everything else) ──
  query_identity:
    label: Query Identity
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/identity
    query_for: product
    help: "Reads the product code, serial and hardware revision; also sizes the channel roster"
  query_site:
    label: Query Site
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/site
    query_for: device_name
  query_state:
    label: Query Device State
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/state
    query_for: device_state
  query_firmware:
    label: Query Firmware
    method: GET
    path: /api/firmware/update/state
    query_for: firmware_version
  query_ssc_version:
    label: Query API Version
    method: GET
    path: /api/ssc/version
    query_for: ssc_schema_version
  query_rf:
    label: Query Frequency Range
    method: GET
    path: /api/rf
    query_for: rf_code
  query_transmission:
    label: Query Transmission Mode
    method: GET
    path: /api/rf/transmission
    query_for: transmission_mode
  query_identification:
    label: Query Identification
    method: GET
    path: /api/device/identification
    query_for: identifying

  # ── Device ──
  identify_on:
    label: Identify Receiver
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/identification
    body: '{"visual": true}'
    help: "Flashes the receiver's display so you can find it in the rack"
    sets: { identifying: true }
  identify_off:
    label: Stop Identifying Receiver
    method: PUT
    path: /api/device/identification
    body: '{"visual": false}'
    sets: { identifying: false }
  set_transmission_mode:
    label: Set Transmission Mode
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/transmission
    body: '{"mode": "{mode}"}'
    help: "Link Density doubles the number of channels that fit in a crowded spectrum; the receiver is briefly Busy while it switches"
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Mode
        values:
          - { value: "Standard", label: "Standard" }
          - { value: "LinkDensity", label: "Link Density" }
    sets: { transmission_mode: "{mode}" }
  encryption_on:
    label: Enable Encryption
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/encryption
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "AES-256 on the radio link; transmitters must be synced afterwards"
    sets: { encryption_enabled: true }
  encryption_off:
    label: Disable Encryption
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/encryption
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    sets: { encryption_enabled: false }

  # ── Receiver channel ──
  set_channel_name:
    label: Set Channel Name
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}
    body: '{"name": "{name}"}'
    help: "Up to eight characters: digits, capitals and a few symbols, as the receiver's display can show"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Name
        pattern: '^[ #*+,;/<=|>0-9A-Z-]{0,8}$'
    sets: { name: "{name}" }
  mute_channel:
    label: Mute Channel
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}
    body: '{"mute": true}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
    sets: { mute: true }
  unmute_channel:
    label: Unmute Channel
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}
    body: '{"mute": false}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
    sets: { mute: false }
  set_channel_gain:
    label: Set Channel Gain
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}
    body: '{"gain": {gain}}'
    help: "-3 to +42 dB in steps of 3 dB; the receiver refuses a value between steps"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      gain:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Gain
        min: -3
        max: 42
        unit: dB
    sets: { gain: "{gain}" }
  set_channel_output_level:
    label: Set Channel Output Level
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}
    body: '{"outputLevel": {level}}'
    help: "-24 to +18 dB in steps of 6 dB; the receiver refuses a value between steps"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Output Level
        min: -24
        max: 18
        unit: dB
    sets: { output_level: "{level}" }
  identify_channel_on:
    label: Identify Channel
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}/identify
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Flashes the channel on the receiver's display"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
    sets: { identifying: true }
  identify_channel_off:
    label: Stop Identifying Channel
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}/identify
    body: '{"enabled": false}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
    sets: { identifying: false }
  restore_channel_audio:
    label: Restore Channel Audio Defaults
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}/restore
    body: '{"mode": "AudioDefault"}'
    help: "Puts the channel's gain, output level and mute back to the factory values"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
  acknowledge_channel_sorting:
    label: Acknowledge Channel Sorting
    method: PUT
    path: /api/channel/{channel}/channelSorting
    body: '{"sorted": true}'
    help: "Clears the receiver's channel-sorting prompt after channels were reordered"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }

  # ── RF ──
  set_channel_frequency:
    label: Set Channel Frequency
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/channels/{channel}/frequency
    body: '{"frequency": {frequency}}'
    help: "In kHz, a multiple of 25 within the receiver's tuning range (see Tuning Range Start and End). The transmitter must be synced afterwards"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Frequency
        unit: kHz
        min: 470000
        max: 1805000
    sets: { frequency_khz: "{frequency}" }
  recall_channel_preset:
    label: Recall Channel Frequency Preset
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/channels/{channel}/preset
    body: '{"type": "{type}", "bank": {bank}, "channel": {preset_channel}}'
    help: "Tunes the channel to a preset from the factory bank or the channel's user bank"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Preset Type
        values:
          - { value: "Factory", label: "Factory bank" }
          - { value: "User", label: "User bank" }
      bank:
        type: integer
        label: Bank
        default: 0
        min: 0
        max: 0
        help: "The receiver has one bank of each type, bank 0"
      preset_channel:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Preset Number
        min: 1
        max: 100
    sets: { preset_type: "{type}", preset_bank: "{bank}", preset_channel: "{preset_channel}" }
  set_channel_user_bank:
    label: Write Channel User Preset Bank
    method: PUT
    path: /api/rf/presets/user/channels/{channel}/banks/0
    body: '{frequencies}'
    help: "Replaces the channel's user frequency bank: a list of 1 to 100 frequencies in kHz, written as [470200, 470400, ...]"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      frequencies:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Frequencies (kHz)
        pattern: '^\[\s*\d+(\s*,\s*\d+){0,99}\s*\]$'

  # ── Sync settings (what a sync writes into the transmitter) ──
  set_channel_sync_mute_config:
    label: Set Sync Mute Mode
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"muteConfig": "{mode}"}'
    help: "What a handheld or bodypack's mute switch does after the next sync"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Mute Mode
        values:
          - { value: "Off", label: "Off" }
          - { value: "RfMute", label: "RF mute" }
          - { value: "AfMute", label: "AF mute" }
    sets: { sync_mute_config: "{mode}" }
  set_channel_sync_cable_emulation:
    label: Set Sync Cable Emulation
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"cableEmulation": "{mode}"}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Cable Emulation
        values: ["Off", "Type1", "Type2", "Type3"]
    sets: { sync_cable_emulation: "{mode}" }
  set_channel_sync_lowcut:
    label: Set Sync Low Cut
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"lowcut": "{lowcut}"}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      lowcut:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Low Cut
        values: ["Off", "30Hz", "60Hz", "80Hz", "100Hz", "120Hz"]
    sets: { sync_lowcut: "{lowcut}" }
  set_channel_sync_lock:
    label: Set Sync Lock
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"lock": {locked}}'
    help: "Whether the transmitter's controls are locked after the next sync"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      locked:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Lock
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "Locked" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Unlocked" }
  set_channel_sync_trim:
    label: Set Sync Trim
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"trim": {trim}}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      trim:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Trim
        min: -12
        max: 6
        unit: dB
    sets: { sync_trim: "{trim}" }
  set_channel_sync_led:
    label: Set Sync LED
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"led": {enabled}}'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      enabled:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: LED
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
  set_channel_sync_mute_config_ts:
    label: Set Sync Table Stand Mute Mode
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}
    body: '{"muteConfigTs": "{mode}"}'
    help: "What a table stand's button does after the next sync"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Table Stand Mute Mode
        values:
          - { value: "AfMute", label: "AF mute" }
          - { value: "Off", label: "Off" }
          - { value: "PTT", label: "Push to talk" }
          - { value: "PTM", label: "Push to mute" }
    sets: { sync_mute_config_ts: "{mode}" }
  set_channel_sync_ignore:
    label: Set Sync Skip
    method: PUT
    path: /api/syncSettings/{channel}/ignore
    body: '{"{setting}": {ignored}}'
    help: "Whether a sync leaves one transmitter setting alone instead of writing it"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
      setting:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Setting
        values:
          - { value: "muteConfig", label: "Mute Mode" }
          - { value: "cableEmulation", label: "Cable Emulation" }
          - { value: "lowcut", label: "Low Cut" }
          - { value: "lock", label: "Lock" }
          - { value: "trim", label: "Trim" }
          - { value: "led", label: "LED" }
          - { value: "name", label: "Name" }
          - { value: "frequency", label: "Frequency" }
      ignored:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: On a Sync
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "Skip it" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Write it" }

  # ── Meter feeds (per channel, at runtime) ──
  channel_meters_on:
    label: Channel Meters On
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/channel/{channel}/signalStrengthIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/signalQualityIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/diversityIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/level"]'
    help: "Starts streaming this channel's RF strength, RF quality, diversity and audio level"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
  channel_meters_off:
    label: Channel Meters Off
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/remove
    body: '["/api/channel/{channel}/signalStrengthIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/signalQualityIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/diversityIndicator", "/api/channel/{channel}/level"]'
    help: "Stops this channel's meter feed"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }

  # ── Subscription session (run by the push block; here so they are visible) ──
  subscribe_device:
    label: "Subscribe: device resources"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/device/state", "/api/device/site", "/api/device/identification", "/api/firmware/update/state", "/api/rf", "/api/rf/transmission", "/api/rf/encryption", "/api/ssc/legacyMode"]'
    help: "Run by the push block on every stream open; nothing to send by hand"
  subscribe_channel:
    label: "Subscribe: one channel"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/channel/{channel}", "/api/channel/{channel}/warnings", "/api/channel/{channel}/identify", "/api/rf/channels/{channel}", "/api/syncSettings/{channel}", "/api/syncSettings/{channel}/ignore"]'
    help: "Run by the push block once per channel on every stream open"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: Channel
        map: { "1": 0, "2": 1, "3": 2, "4": 3 }
  subscribe_transmitters:
    label: "Subscribe: transmitters"
    method: PUT
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}/add
    body: '["/api/transmitters"]'
    help: "Run by the push block on every stream open; covers every linked transmitter, now and later"
  end_subscription:
    label: "Subscribe: end session"
    method: DELETE
    path: /api/ssc/state/subscriptions/{push_session}
    help: "Run by the push block when the device is disconnected on purpose"

# ── Responses ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every body is JSON, so every rule is json: true and all of them run
# against every body. Two shapes arrive:
#   - a polled GET answers with the bare resource ({"state": ..}) — those
#     rules are scoped with require: to a key unique to the resource, since
#     several resources share field names (state, enabled);
#   - the subscription stream sends {"<resource path>": {..}} (SSCv2 spec,
#     "Subscription notification syntax"), so those rules read the path
#     as the leading JSON key. A path only ever appears in stream bodies,
#     so they need no require:. Per-channel paths carry the channel index,
#     which is what routes each value to its child.
# The encryption and legacy-mode bodies are both {"enabled": ..} and cannot
# be told apart bare, so they are read from the stream only.
responses:
  # ── Polled bodies ──
  # /api/device/identity (also sizes the roster from the product code)
  - json: true
    require: product
    set:
      product: "product"
      model: { key: "product", map: { "EWDX2CHS": "EW-DX EM 2", "EWDX2CHDS": "EW-DX EM 2 Dante", "EWDX4CHDS": "EW-DX EM 4 Dante" } }
      channel_count_reported: { key: "product", type: integer, map: { "EWDX2CHS": 2, "EWDX2CHDS": 2, "EWDX4CHDS": 4 } }
      serial: "serial"
      hardware_revision: "hardwareRevision"
      vendor: "vendor"
  # /api/device/site
  - json: true
    require: deviceName
    set:
      device_name: "deviceName"
      location: "location"
      position: "position"
  # /api/device/state
  - json: true
    require: warnings
    set:
      device_state: "state"
      device_warning_count: "warnings"
  # /api/firmware/update/state
  - json: true
    require: deviceVersion
    set:
      firmware_version: "deviceVersion"
      dante_version: "danteVersion"
      firmware_update_state: "state"
      firmware_update_progress: "progress"
      firmware_last_status: "lastStatus"
  # /api/ssc/version
  - json: true
    require: schema
    set:
      ssc_protocol_version: "protocol"
      ssc_schema_version: "schema"
  # /api/rf
  - json: true
    require: ranges
    set:
      rf_code: "code"
      rf_range_count: "ranges"
      rf_range_start_khz: "ranges.0.start"
      rf_range_end_khz: "ranges.0.end"
      rf_range_step_khz: "ranges.0.stepSize"
  # /api/rf/transmission
  - json: true
    require: presetSpacing
    set:
      transmission_mode: "mode"
      preset_spacing_khz: "presetSpacing"
  # /api/device/identification
  - json: true
    require: visual
    set:
      identifying: "visual"

  # ── Stream bodies, device level ──
  # /api/device/state
  - json: true
    set:
      device_state: "/api/device/state.state"
      device_warning_count: "/api/device/state.warnings"
  # /api/device/site
  - json: true
    set:
      device_name: "/api/device/site.deviceName"
      location: "/api/device/site.location"
      position: "/api/device/site.position"
  # /api/device/identification
  - json: true
    set:
      identifying: "/api/device/identification.visual"
  # /api/firmware/update/state
  - json: true
    set:
      firmware_version: "/api/firmware/update/state.deviceVersion"
      dante_version: "/api/firmware/update/state.danteVersion"
      firmware_update_state: "/api/firmware/update/state.state"
      firmware_update_progress: "/api/firmware/update/state.progress"
      firmware_last_status: "/api/firmware/update/state.lastStatus"
  # /api/rf
  - json: true
    set:
      rf_code: "/api/rf.code"
      rf_range_count: "/api/rf.ranges"
      rf_range_start_khz: "/api/rf.ranges.0.start"
      rf_range_end_khz: "/api/rf.ranges.0.end"
      rf_range_step_khz: "/api/rf.ranges.0.stepSize"
  # /api/rf/transmission
  - json: true
    set:
      transmission_mode: "/api/rf/transmission.mode"
      preset_spacing_khz: "/api/rf/transmission.presetSpacing"
  # /api/rf/encryption
  - json: true
    set:
      encryption_enabled: "/api/rf/encryption.enabled"
  # /api/ssc/legacyMode
  - json: true
    set:
      legacy_mode_enabled: "/api/ssc/legacyMode.enabled"

  # ── Stream bodies, per channel (the path carries the channel index) ──
  # /api/channel/{n}
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: channel
        id: 1
        state:
          name: "/api/channel/0.name"
          mute: "/api/channel/0.mute"
          gain: "/api/channel/0.gain"
          output_level: "/api/channel/0.outputLevel"
          mate: "/api/channel/0.mates.0"
          audio_output: "/api/channel/0.audio.0"
      - type: channel
        id: 2
        state:
          name: "/api/channel/1.name"
          mute: "/api/channel/1.mute"
          gain: "/api/channel/1.gain"
          output_level: "/api/channel/1.outputLevel"
          mate: "/api/channel/1.mates.0"
          audio_output: "/api/channel/1.audio.0"
      - type: channel
        id: 3
        state:
          name: "/api/channel/2.name"
          mute: "/api/channel/2.mute"
          gain: "/api/channel/2.gain"
          output_level: "/api/channel/2.outputLevel"
          mate: "/api/channel/2.mates.0"
          audio_output: "/api/channel/2.audio.0"
      - type: channel
        id: 4
        state:
          name: "/api/channel/3.name"
          mute: "/api/channel/3.mute"
          gain: "/api/channel/3.gain"
          output_level: "/api/channel/3.outputLevel"
          mate: "/api/channel/3.mates.0"
          audio_output: "/api/channel/3.audio.0"
  # /api/channel/{n}/warnings: an array of flag names, one boolean each
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: channel
        id: 1
        state:
          aes256_error: { key: "/api/channel/0/warnings", contains: "Aes256Error" }
          low_signal: { key: "/api/channel/0/warnings", contains: "LowSignal" }
          no_link: { key: "/api/channel/0/warnings", contains: "NoLink" }
          rf_peak: { key: "/api/channel/0/warnings", contains: "RfPeak" }
          af_peak: { key: "/api/channel/0/warnings", contains: "AfPeak" }
      - type: channel
        id: 2
        state:
          aes256_error: { key: "/api/channel/1/warnings", contains: "Aes256Error" }
          low_signal: { key: "/api/channel/1/warnings", contains: "LowSignal" }
          no_link: { key: "/api/channel/1/warnings", contains: "NoLink" }
          rf_peak: { key: "/api/channel/1/warnings", contains: "RfPeak" }
          af_peak: { key: "/api/channel/1/warnings", contains: "AfPeak" }
      - type: channel
        id: 3
        state:
          aes256_error: { key: "/api/channel/2/warnings", contains: "Aes256Error" }
          low_signal: { key: "/api/channel/2/warnings", contains: "LowSignal" }
          no_link: { key: "/api/channel/2/warnings", contains: "NoLink" }
          rf_peak: { key: "/api/channel/2/warnings", contains: "RfPeak" }
          af_peak: { key: "/api/channel/2/warnings", contains: "AfPeak" }
      - type: channel
        id: 4
        state:
          aes256_error: { key: "/api/channel/3/warnings", contains: "Aes256Error" }
          low_signal: { key: "/api/channel/3/warnings", contains: "LowSignal" }
          no_link: { key: "/api/channel/3/warnings", contains: "NoLink" }
          rf_peak: { key: "/api/channel/3/warnings", contains: "RfPeak" }
          af_peak: { key: "/api/channel/3/warnings", contains: "AfPeak" }
  # /api/channel/{n}/identify
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: channel
        id: 1
        state:
          identifying: "/api/channel/0/identify.enabled"
      - type: channel
        id: 2
        state:
          identifying: "/api/channel/1/identify.enabled"
      - type: channel
        id: 3
        state:
          identifying: "/api/channel/2/identify.enabled"
      - type: channel
        id: 4
        state:
          identifying: "/api/channel/3/identify.enabled"
  # /api/rf/channels/{n}
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: channel
        id: 1
        state:
          frequency_khz: "/api/rf/channels/0.frequency"
          preset_type: "/api/rf/channels/0.presets.type"
          preset_bank: "/api/rf/channels/0.presets.bank"
          preset_channel: "/api/rf/channels/0.presets.channel"
      - type: channel
        id: 2
        state:
          frequency_khz: "/api/rf/channels/1.frequency"
          preset_type: "/api/rf/channels/1.presets.type"
          preset_bank: "/api/rf/channels/1.presets.bank"
          preset_channel: "/api/rf/channels/1.presets.channel"
      - type: channel
        id: 3
        state:
          frequency_khz: "/api/rf/channels/2.frequency"
          preset_type: "/api/rf/channels/2.presets.type"
          preset_bank: "/api/rf/channels/2.presets.bank"
          preset_channel: "/api/rf/channels/2.presets.channel"
      - type: channel
        id: 4
        state:
          frequency_khz: "/api/rf/channels/3.frequency"
          preset_type: "/api/rf/channels/3.presets.type"
          preset_bank: "/api/rf/channels/3.presets.bank"
          preset_channel: "/api/rf/channels/3.presets.channel"
  # /api/syncSettings/{n}
  - json: true
    child_set:
      - type: channel
        id: 1
        state:
          sync_mute_config: "/api/syncSettings/0.muteConfig"
